<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 11 August, from 117 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cilicia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">117 <span class="tih-ago">1,909 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hadrian is proclaimed Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days after Trajan's death in Cilicia, the army in Syria hailed Hadrian as emperor. He abandoned Trajan's eastern conquests and consolidated the frontiers, building Hadrian's Wall in Britain.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1492 <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rodrigo Borgia is elected Pope Alexander VI</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Spanish cardinal Rodrigo Borgia was elected pope, amid accusations of bribery. His reign became notorious for nepotism and for advancing his children, among them Cesare and Lucrezia Borgia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1919 <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Ebert signs the Weimar Constitution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Friedrich Ebert signed the constitution of the new German republic, with universal suffrage and a strong president. Its emergency powers were later exploited in Hitler's rise to power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1960 <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chad becomes independent from France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chad gained independence, with François Tombalbaye as its first president. It was one of 17 African countries to win independence in 1960, the 'Year of Africa'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1965 <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Watts riots erupt in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A traffic stop in the Watts district sparked six days of unrest in which 34 people died. The riots exposed deep anger over poverty and policing in America's segregated cities.</p></div></li></ol>
